1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
1. Little Hoppers for Little Andare

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:10,560
When Andare was a little boy, he loved eating hoppers for breakfast.

3
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:15,000
Every morning, his mother would give him twenty panam to buy some.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,560
Andare would take the money, head over to the hopper lady, and bring back four hoppers.

5
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:26,720
Sometimes the hoppers she made came out way too small, and those tiny ones wouldn't sell.

6
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:28,860
So what did she do with the leftovers?

7
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:33,660
She sold all the tiny hoppers to little Andare.

8
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:39,540
For a few days, Andare watched her pull this trick, quietly nursing a grudge.

9
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:47,260
Finally, one day, little Andare said to himself, "She gives me tiny hoppers every single day.

10
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:50,180
I'm going to teach her a good lesson."

11
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:56,140
Sure enough, that day too, she handed him four tiny hoppers for his twenty panam.

12
00:00:56,780 --> 00:01:00,500
"Auntie, why are these hoppers so tiny?"

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:01,260
Andare asked.

14
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:07,420
The hopper lady replied, "Well, Andare, you're small, aren't you?

15
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:11,460
It's much easier for little kids to eat little hoppers.

16
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:16,380
Not only that, since they're lighter, they're easier for you to carry home, too."

17
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:20,340
"Oh, is that so?"

18
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:25,740
Andare said, tossing some coins into her basket before grabbing his hoppers and running off toward home.

19
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:29,900
The hopper lady looked down into the basket.

20
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:36,860
Instead of four five-panam coins, there were only four one-panam coins sitting there.

21
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:38,180
She was furious.

22
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:40,300
"Stop right there, Andare!

23
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:42,500
You're short on money here.

24
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,220
Why did you drop these tiny coins and run off?"

25
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:46,300
she yelled angrily.

26
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:50,900
"When it's less money, it's easier for you to count, Auntie.

27
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:54,260
And since the coins are tiny, they're easier for you to keep,"

28
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:57,780
Andare called back, running all the way home without looking back.
